"Hold a steady pulse when the kick leaves the quarter-note grid." = "Hold a steady pulse when the kick leaves the quarter-note grid.";
"The second kick is just before beat 3. A silent downbeat is intentional; do not fill it with an extra kick." = "The second kick is just before beat 3. A silent downbeat is intentional; do not fill it with an extra kick.";
"Keep lesson 1 unchanged and add a right-hand rim on 4 a. The hat on 4 & comes first, then the rim, then the kick on the next 1." = "Keep lesson 1 unchanged and add a right-hand rim on 4 a. The hat on 4 & comes first, then the rim, then the kick on the next 1.";
"Add a pickup at the end of the bar without shortening the bar." = "Add a pickup at the end of the bar without shortening the bar.";
"The rim is a sixteenth before the next kick. Do not press rim and kick together." = "The rim is a sixteenth before the next kick. Do not press rim and kick together.";
"Alternate two bars. In bar 1, the middle kick is on 2 a; in bar 2 it moves earlier to 2 &. Hats, snares and the final rim stay the same. Learn the kick changes alone, then add the other layers." = "Alternate two bars. In bar 1, the middle kick is on 2 a; in bar 2 it moves earlier to 2 &. Hats, snares and the final rim stay the same. Learn the kick changes alone, then add the other layers.";
"Alternate two kick shapes while the other parts stay steady." = "Alternate two kick shapes while the other parts stay steady.";
"Bar 2 has kick and hat together on 2 &. It is a deliberate change, not a timing mistake." = "Bar 2 has kick and hat together on 2 &. It is a deliberate change, not a timing mistake.";
"Keep alternating the two kick shapes across four bars. In bar 4, leave out the final closed hat and play rim answers on 4 e and 4 a. Count the missing hat silently. Return to the kick on 1. Practise bar 4 as a section, then finish a full run." = "Keep alternating the two kick shapes across four bars. In bar 4, leave out the final closed hat and play rim answers on 4 e and 4 a. Count the missing hat silently. Return to the kick on 1. Practise bar 4 as a section, then finish a full run.";
"Keep a four-bar form through an intentional gap and a rim answer." = "Keep a four-bar form through an intentional gap and a rim answer.";
"The final bar replaces the hat on 4 & with silence. An extra hat there counts as an extra hit." = "The final bar replaces the hat on 4 & with silence. An extra hat there counts as an extra hit.";
"Start with a four-beat kick. Put the rim on 2 & and on beat 4. Count every beat even though the rim gives the pattern a different shape." = "Start with a four-beat kick. Put the rim on 2 & and on beat 4. Count every beat even though the rim gives the pattern a different shape.";
"Place a syncopated rim over a steady dance pulse." = "Place a syncopated rim over a steady dance pulse.";
"The first rim is between beats 2 and 3. The second rim lands together with the kick on beat 4." = "The first rim is between beats 2 and 3. The second rim lands together with the kick on beat 4.";
"Switch to a clap on 2 and 4. Keep open hats on every & and add short closed hats on 1 a and 3 a. Bar 2 ends with one extra kick on 4 a. Listen to each layer first; this first exercise uses a straight grid." = "Switch to a clap on 2 and 4. Keep open hats on every & and add short closed hats on 1 a and 3 a. Bar 2 ends with one extra kick on 4 a. Listen to each layer first; this first exercise uses a straight grid.";
"Keep a dance pulse under a skippy two-bar hat and kick phrase." = "Keep a dance pulse under a skippy two-bar hat and kick phrase.";
"Each closed hat follows an open hat by one sixteenth. Let the final kick of bar 2 lead into the next bar; do not merge the two kicks." = "Each closed hat follows an open hat by one sixteenth. Let the final kick of bar 2 lead into the next bar; do not merge the two kicks.";
"Play the two-bar idea as a four-bar phrase. Bar 3 adds one quiet closed hat on 2 a. In bar 4, replace the clap on 4 with a short snare answer on 4, 4 & and 4 a. Keep the kick under it, then return to 1. This is a straight-grid foundation; fine shuffle is not scored separately." = "Play the two-bar idea as a four-bar phrase. Bar 3 adds one quiet closed hat on 2 a. In bar 4, replace the clap on 4 with a short snare answer on 4, 4 & and 4 a. Keep the kick under it, then return to 1. This is a straight-grid foundation; fine shuffle is not scored separately.";
"Finish a four-bar club phrase with a snare answer and a clean restart." = "Finish a four-bar club phrase with a snare answer and a clean restart.";
"Kick and snare land together on beat 4. The following two snares are not evenly spaced triplets." = "Kick and snare land together on beat 4. The following two snares are not evenly spaced triplets.";
