"Auto uses Virtuosity for jazz, New Orleans and blues; the World palette for Latin, Afro-Cuban, Afrobeat, Highlife and Middle Eastern lessons; 808 for electronic styles, Jersey club and footwork; AVL acoustic for other genres. You can choose any palette manually. World keeps acoustic drums and adds recorded shaker, woodblock and cowbell; it does not change a snare into a conga." = "Auto uses Virtuosity for jazz, New Orleans and blues; the World palette for Latin, Afro-Cuban, Afrobeat, Highlife and Middle Eastern lessons; 808 for electronic styles, Jersey club and footwork; AVL acoustic for other genres. You can choose any palette manually. World keeps acoustic drums and adds recorded shaker, woodblock and cowbell; it does not change a snare into a conga.";
"AVL and the selected Virtuosity drums use five recorded dynamic layers. Virtuosity cymbals and percussion use their original velocity splits and alternate actual recorded takes; the shaker has one velocity layer. The 808 responds to MIDI velocity through volume. Keyboard input uses a fixed velocity. Samples load before the lesson count-in begins. Jazz downloads about 64 MB on first use; decoded samples are reused during this session. Shared files are loaded once across palettes. A closed hi-hat cuts off an open hi-hat." = "AVL and the selected Virtuosity drums use five recorded dynamic layers. Virtuosity cymbals and percussion use their original velocity splits and alternate actual recorded takes; the shaker has one velocity layer. The 808 responds to MIDI velocity through volume. Keyboard input uses a fixed velocity. Samples load before the lesson count-in begins. Jazz downloads about 64 MB on first use; decoded samples are reused during this session. Shared files are loaded once across palettes. A closed hi-hat cuts off an open hi-hat.";
"The eight-pad layout preserves the usual positions wherever possible. Positions unused by the lesson can carry its additional instruments; the pad labels show each assignment. Six advanced lessons use one snare pad for both hands. Every hit and its timing stays intact. Map the eight physical pads once; their MIDI map is saved separately from the sixteen-pad layout." = "The eight-pad layout preserves the usual positions wherever possible. Positions unused by the lesson can carry its additional instruments; the pad labels show each assignment. Six advanced lessons use one snare pad for both hands. Every hit and its timing stays intact. Map the eight physical pads once; their MIDI map is saved separately from the sixteen-pad layout.";
", recorded by Glen MacArthur. CC BY-SA 3.0. The audio is unchanged; 65 files were selected and renamed. Wood uses a stick click, Shaker uses maracas and Open hat uses the recorded hat swish." = ", recorded by Glen MacArthur. CC BY-SA 3.0. The audio is unchanged; 65 files were selected and renamed. Wood uses a stick click, Shaker uses maracas and Open hat uses the recorded hat swish.";
", Michael Fischer / Technopolis, TR-808 Sound Sample Set 1.0.0 (1994). CC0. Wood uses claves; Ride uses a short 808 cymbal setting. House and techno currently use 808; a dedicated 909 kit is not included." = ", Michael Fischer / Technopolis, TR-808 Sound Sample Set 1.0.0 (1994). CC0. Wood uses claves; Ride uses a short 808 cymbal setting. House and techno currently use 808; a dedicated 909 kit is not included.";
", Versilian Studios and Karoryfer Samples, performed by Austin McMahon. CC0 for Virtuosity recordings; the clap uses the existing AVL sample under CC BY-SA 3.0. Includes stereo cymbals with four recorded variants for closed hat, ride and crash, three for open hat. A selected palette rather than the full library and microphone mixer." = ", Versilian Studios and Karoryfer Samples, performed by Austin McMahon. CC0 for Virtuosity recordings; the clap uses the existing AVL sample under CC BY-SA 3.0. Includes stereo cymbals with four recorded variants for closed hat, ride and crash, three for open hat. A selected palette rather than the full library and microphone mixer.";
"combines AVL drums with Virtuosity shaker, low woodblock and cowbell. The auxiliary percussion has two recorded variants. Pad names and lesson rhythms stay the same." = "combines AVL drums with Virtuosity shaker, low woodblock and cowbell. The auxiliary percussion has two recorded variants. Pad names and lesson rhythms stay the same.";
